  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Each available game lists its player range, and only groups within that range begin play; guests can wait for another opening.\", \"decision\": \"How should guests form tables for the next games?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteer teachers announce the games they can start, and interested guests gather before the host confirms player numbers. A brief face-to-face invitation helps guests assess the group and ask questions before committing to a table.\nGuests place their names beside available games until each table reaches its listed player range. People choose directly among current openings, and the visible names show which games are close to being ready.\nThe host asks ready guests for two game preferences and proposes tables within the listed player ranges. Several preferences can be considered together before guests accept an available seat or choose to wait."
    }
  ],
